      "writtenOn": "2022-12-28T19:33:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Skia currently requires a two\u0027s-complement little-endian CPU. It might be centrally documented already, but it\u0027s definitely called out in the code in various existing places:\n\nhttps://osscs.corp.google.com/skia/skia/+/main:include/core/SkTypes.h;l\u003d225;drc\u003d2b8b2146765157b40197e0fd491402b69202968c\n\nhttps://osscs.corp.google.com/skia/skia/+/main:src/core/SkMathPriv.h;l\u003d80-83;drc\u003dcd938c5b0fe635a652fa21250f4849a4f746a108\n\nI could imagine a world where big-endian returns somehow (I was a Mac guy way before they went to Intel), but I don\u0027t think one\u0027s-complement is ever coming back around :)",
